{"objects":[{"id":"flow","instance":"instance--b96dad5f-c519-5a1f-a718-912ca4a86c02","objects":["attack-action--1","attack-action--2","attack-action--3","attack-action--4","attack-action--5","attack-action--6","attack-action--7","attack-action--8","attack-action--9","attack-action--10","attack-condition--1","attack-condition--2","attack-operator--1","attack-operator--2","email-message--1","instance--9e152109-b123-5ad0-bd9a-d94f1439c8e8","instance--0eaca345-1f2b-546b-afb8-37d3c0f945ef","url--1","file--1","instance--c071eb6a-7d83-5642-b84b-9c5b277175c0","instance--b3fb9a46-4198-5d4c-b97e-8d46a5869af2","file--2","software--1","instance--6c2fa7a5-752c-5112-80ce-0af709e70546","instance--5c74b289-c39a-5d62-b610-c866f2ef5e82","instance--f825654a-7f81-50f7-a4e3-715efc45ad7a","instance--384798bd-a84b-5feb-8d38-7f9d0a087f11","instance--057c9c6b-5f9d-5a42-a700-338d5f0eb74a","instance--a6618e5f-2d2d-55c4-9d60-5edfe63f3ef7","instance--b6d82c28-0a68-5c6f-b058-c1e072f51852","instance--0dca9c99-f5f1-58a0-acdf-40197f3f2c69","instance--3bb881aa-a5ab-51ba-b53d-89d26964ce7d","instance--5824580a-ff0f-5565-bba6-97a7c9ed3a5e","instance--7cc46cbd-beb8-54eb-aef6-32656d039f20","instance--d23a7e3b-28ba-5c82-b661-c8eb109d42d1","instance--b6301b03-e1db-5d07-8b01-10b9d63abc5a","instance--270cbdbf-5237-582b-8769-006040705683","instance--26a4f1bd-fd59-5282-bccf-b30643939219","instance--b8c05c4e-eaa8-5707-be20-b5c030a4e132","instance--f73cb290-6345-5dc5-af08-9677f9bb8434","instance--4a2e5ab5-1f48-53b2-b16b-c737e0b3bd7b","instance--111a564d-0912-5013-a0f8-2216c50150b8","instance--03a46723-5271-5abc-85a3-2206cd087765","instance--d0f200db-7b2a-50a9-9430-330537193c08","instance--9f9958fd-1d8b-567e-b94c-8c1e28e650cf","instance--4174b963-9347-5fe4-94bd-81b81939df38","instance--8c2d2c4c-bd94-5aa3-a7cd-61ba35e21a7c","instance--6b5651cb-5932-55cd-9dbf-5472ebd10b9f","instance--d6f6eee0-de81-5882-b0d9-43f4e8ea3190","instance--878c95d7-7602-587d-9226-52424b74acef"],"properties":[["name","Agent Tesla infection and data theft flow"],["description","Behavioral infection flow for Agent Tesla Keylogger as described in the source narrative."],["scope","incident"],["author",[["name","James Arndt"]]],["external_references",[["item-1",[["source_name","cofense.com"],["url","https://cofense.com/blog/the-rise-of-agent-tesla-understanding-the-notorious-keylogger/"]]]]]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--ad592d05-6969-5b51-98a8-1ad9b6aab896","120":"instance--5850a8f4-8241-5e73-9bf0-dcd376cd5025","150":"instance--0da1498f-3beb-5916-a249-e0410a4a81e4","180":"instance--d3632784-7391-5a29-83e2-edab51db56c6","210":"instance--8bc47ca5-ca73-5a04-a9ea-918608f10871","240":"instance--6546eef6-c5ad-516e-a417-89916e651648","270":"instance--244e5a69-f465-564e-9d2c-93d4da44fc57","30":"instance--6a1fca3c-fdb6-536a-bbea-61ac2349a700","300":"instance--043a5b44-2864-5565-abce-1909204e5485","330":"instance--e10eb918-2b0b-56f4-9c82-f345ce21276c","60":"instance--33a99d1b-dad8-51f6-be74-e1614db9151b","90":"instance--380c79e9-b1eb-547c-bf01-a011db1201c1"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--1","properties":[["name","Deliver malicious attachment or URL"],["description","As shown in Figure 2, an Agent Tesla Keylogger executable is typically delivered via a direct attachment to an email. The CVE-2017-11882 vulnerability, attached DotNET Loaders, and embedded URLs follow as popular delivery methods."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0001","technique":"T1566.001"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--4f4d03a8-4502-5010-997b-9943e254395b","120":"instance--cefe62ac-5b6e-5ead-84fc-b4c632913a73","150":"instance--4d07a740-2467-5b95-ac8d-4a2ee8edd11e","180":"instance--1205f03c-a457-5a0b-87ef-3bbb7aac110f","210":"instance--96e7dc6a-9f86-5f69-8d45-a566303cd4c0","240":"instance--66237af6-bb19-5a51-9fa2-cbc4a96186f5","270":"instance--836dfd42-b475-50ca-9acf-4f11bd32b89f","30":"instance--efe92997-cc5c-538a-90bc-c09ffb1379f4","300":"instance--9c4a24ae-1426-5cb5-9d7c-792e6dd325b7","330":"instance--06c6a74a-ca7d-5703-88ea-a06a0933d21a","60":"instance--5e4f84e5-56b7-5b8f-9bc3-b4d59d371123","90":"instance--019deb6a-bab3-57db-9a53-11e3564bf7a4"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--2","properties":[["name","Exploit CVE-2017-11882 document"],["description","In March 2020, during the beginning of worldwide lockdowns due to COVID-19, threat actors used COVID-19-themed phishing lures to spread Agent Tesla Keylogger. Its popularity surged in the third and fourth quarters of 2020 and the first two quarters of 2021. Office documents with macros and malicious .rtf documents exploiting CVE-2017-11882 were often used to download and execute Agent Tesla Keylogger."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0002","technique":"T1203"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--0ce35aea-35a2-52ae-a67b-985306bdefe7","120":"instance--312639d5-e6d9-57b1-850d-28f0a1eac2f6","150":"instance--9551a25e-2558-512e-9894-dd64a8d662bf","180":"instance--403becce-e0ad-5dcd-bc14-7c00453907da","210":"instance--2305f501-2712-5ec6-9d4e-1371b011e937","240":"instance--cf1b8cf6-1cbd-5afb-b653-aa693889dab5","270":"instance--1d3dc59a-40a0-5670-aa3e-1304ff762003","30":"instance--77063d4f-503a-5e9b-b622-15aa2cc6a8e7","300":"instance--beaab67f-8a54-5982-8c5d-9d2ed2d42c9f","330":"instance--4d3274ff-ef14-5a53-99be-01575194a98e","60":"instance--4154a6bf-290b-5fce-a557-5dc0f3e700fb","90":"instance--2992bc0b-df57-54e5-a17b-03a964338c09"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--3","properties":[["name","Unpack or decode stage two"],["description","Stage one of an Agent Tesla Keylogger infection typically begins with either a packed PE file or one that has been written in .NET. In either case, the first step is to unpack or decode a large chunk of data before stage two can be executed. Figure 7 below is an example of the PE file being written in .NET. The resource contains a long string of characters. The code replaces certain characters with others and stores the result in an array. This array becomes the second stage of the infection process when it is executed."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0005","technique":"T1140"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--0f6e4da7-a5f4-54d7-866f-3bc6e8bcb019","120":"instance--015254b5-0906-577e-b3e3-3899f837d118","150":"instance--f7af5b8c-330a-58d5-b0da-a3d5f0bc6ad0","180":"instance--9f27ab21-2382-567d-b022-74ad5a29bd08","210":"instance--d799eb0a-7600-5b1a-a298-c47a78ceae4b","240":"instance--911c2c52-5974-5e08-b0b6-a9084d57c6ee","270":"instance--286444b4-97a1-58cd-9ca3-cffa04a15351","30":"instance--92192c38-5143-50e0-8c39-a96ea86e32e2","300":"instance--82bb3de0-bea5-5651-a1de-583283258c6d","330":"instance--4f0945c8-f644-50ce-8796-fea52a29dda1","60":"instance--16c43a2d-7356-521d-a507-5922e2c3337b","90":"instance--abce5c62-339a-5ed5-a0b8-dd66136cfe2f"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--4","properties":[["name","Check for debugger"],["description","Once the second stage is running, it performs some basic checks to see if it is running in a debugger, to determine whether it is being scrutinized by a security analyst."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0005","technique":"T1622"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--a469636c-0cb2-50b9-92f9-644c8aa98197","120":"instance--d57b3a21-e910-5879-8148-40165cea451a","150":"instance--58250ef4-5bb4-5bf3-b33e-89493bbb395d","180":"instance--3e769cf2-c1e5-5d2e-81d4-892f48ce4d86","210":"instance--f6499e41-749c-5d7f-9346-96c08d0d5dfd","240":"instance--d9dcdfc8-5f42-546a-803a-0efcd5d4cf91","270":"instance--c9afd0f6-97ce-57b2-9d60-3557b6214809","30":"instance--75f82155-f5ff-5619-8bf8-aae22937cab0","300":"instance--25e2d26e-1b35-56bd-b9aa-096c2d3b0e3c","330":"instance--e0483688-da10-5376-8cf2-050bcc3b70f0","60":"instance--1293d9cc-16b2-5c67-a453-bd144aab133a","90":"instance--2b43cd52-10db-5b15-8ad5-c4b59496528b"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--5","properties":[["name","Gather host information"],["description","If it determines that it is not being analyzed, it then gathers information about the infected endpoint, such as the MAC address, processor information, and motherboard serial number. This information is sent back to the attacker."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0007","technique":"T1082"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--54fc1f38-f4e3-523e-b07c-73889b0d8df7","120":"instance--9cf45948-7040-5d7a-a1d5-3cb4db0c1af6","150":"instance--13bb13cc-e02b-51d2-8d7d-40e5613b6e5a","180":"instance--e33bc6ee-771e-54fe-a772-74dfdaad420d","210":"instance--286f51a3-8fc6-55ec-978e-8b05ebda3655","240":"instance--14659696-be77-5460-beb1-4b5eac126e43","270":"instance--f48ed1a6-2895-5cd2-9b1c-e30ac2bc8921","30":"instance--7b803e61-16ac-5720-92cd-8f2a456a52b7","300":"instance--76c24361-5143-5c43-8e4d-707c619e6038","330":"instance--f395cfc7-395a-5001-9552-a4fec6dbc53a","60":"instance--760885bb-9294-5a5b-93a2-a410e1ea4112","90":"instance--8e0d1a12-8611-598d-9a7d-40f2525e4781"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--6","properties":[["name","Exfiltrate host information"],["description","If it determines that it is not being analyzed, it then gathers information about the infected endpoint, such as the MAC address, processor information, and motherboard serial number. This information is sent back to the attacker."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0010","technique":"T1041"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--7cccbcd0-a724-54fb-be4f-ac523d26f7d0","120":"instance--738e44b2-1357-5eb3-82bd-8a0ce8942b72","150":"instance--d31f4735-6339-5929-8d7c-d30863cf166f","180":"instance--2252393d-d801-5931-ad38-4b53374a9880","210":"instance--065b5ad5-023a-5336-b458-e9c9dcda2976","240":"instance--5ea0dd2b-5eac-51f8-855a-4cbcb801bc2d","270":"instance--bba66874-a069-56c6-bb95-967cb3cefc9e","30":"instance--6377c09d-ecb4-5567-a2f4-4dde56ff4f98","300":"instance--ede3430f-b16b-58ae-be71-1d1f1a194336","330":"instance--7772f482-8ee2-569a-b600-7528c065d4e0","60":"instance--98139a98-16b0-54fe-8c77-3473c1b520cd","90":"instance--5cb9cc95-e190-5a68-985d-0a94d39299e6"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--7","properties":[["name","Monitor keystrokes"],["description","Based upon how it was originally configured (Figure 3), Agent Tesla will start monitoring keystrokes, check for the existence of applications from which to steal passwords, and exfiltrate screenshots at regular intervals."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0009","technique":"T1056.001"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--5150f7cc-6f25-5eb3-a6fc-5099ced4caf4","120":"instance--64a408ce-c543-55d6-a9dd-206ce7cadbb2","150":"instance--1b71e413-cfd2-528c-8792-dc7dd1bb9938","180":"instance--aa12ce11-0165-52b6-b72d-e4d9070e9fbb","210":"instance--5d8b0f08-14bc-58f4-9316-b25a92dd09a6","240":"instance--34f96b84-9453-53f2-ae07-d28c04665e6c","270":"instance--415f1d54-1cd4-5ba7-8071-4aa99bc946ac","30":"instance--18834cac-b4c4-57b0-88ea-5a62fdb27cf9","300":"instance--de4f9957-1ac6-5782-86ea-f1a3b6a9ad13","330":"instance--8eff940b-86bb-556f-8c85-c7c47577b3ed","60":"instance--14a123fd-5626-5e69-8257-6dcd64c28ec0","90":"instance--02294ff1-7261-5db8-8e0d-b9e818922053"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--8","properties":[["name","Check for password source applications"],["description","Based upon how it was originally configured (Figure 3), Agent Tesla will start monitoring keystrokes, check for the existence of applications from which to steal passwords, and exfiltrate screenshots at regular intervals."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0007","technique":"T1518"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--180f2983-9c1a-56f4-99d6-c990125f7baa","120":"instance--c7f65318-7600-57f4-a8ac-992357e695ff","150":"instance--95523e1a-0a1d-52ef-944c-23f9cbc50233","180":"instance--bc8eb48d-411d-5877-aa9b-966476b71207","210":"instance--4cc5026e-07f9-5327-9912-5d278a0a3321","240":"instance--d6a7d51d-39a4-5eb3-8831-f23437781b95","270":"instance--cac30e05-5f01-5b4f-b5c0-6b975297df2d","30":"instance--cb0751b0-c027-5895-a460-a72e48920c71","300":"instance--f41cdc1f-abb7-5ff7-81c2-bf2235a7faab","330":"instance--b114cbda-9ec8-5612-b2f8-93c36811cafb","60":"instance--f28e5296-2041-5fe9-992d-4c70d549191e","90":"instance--3ea39244-da0f-5435-8745-f2afa8b13872"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--9","properties":[["name","Capture and exfiltrate screenshots"],["description","Based upon how it was originally configured (Figure 3), Agent Tesla will start monitoring keystrokes, check for the existence of applications from which to steal passwords, and exfiltrate screenshots at regular intervals."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0009","technique":"T1113"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--db5fab04-54d4-5eec-a429-185861eb2719","120":"instance--985391bd-d017-5935-ab31-3b4b56331b02","150":"instance--092bb98d-fc30-5f69-b6b7-e3024f3ec65a","180":"instance--755129e6-612e-5b63-a780-1c886d98909b","210":"instance--431723d9-dd8c-5190-9dab-6f346173c044","240":"instance--5b9fb821-54fe-5f22-bba3-038263245910","270":"instance--3c6777cb-6430-544b-b31a-01b198524553","30":"instance--c070071b-a9a3-52fe-8956-a51744db200b","300":"instance--a9a4289c-d995-5783-9544-a8b45052eb56","330":"instance--344009cc-e024-5c68-9246-51e85e00d45c","60":"instance--86c77621-2c1d-59c3-b398-e62f4b48a3dd","90":"instance--67627b08-1913-5f3d-8318-52d3bda9c1c3"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--10","properties":[["name","Use registry keys for persistence"],["description","Figure 10 above showed evidence of how Agent Tesla Keylogger is using the and registry keys to establish persistence. Changes to those and other common registry keys used for malware persistence should be monitored."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0003","technique":"T1547.001"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--35652c79-2c41-5d60-81ba-b5e47aa554bf","120":"instance--53906203-fffb-5af3-b112-44a9b4b49b8f","150":"instance--465fbc8a-7b4c-569f-be00-c0fbc137fcfc","180":"instance--a653c96b-3673-5dfa-968e-188fffe4cc04","210":"instance--6a344cf5-bd5c-52db-84f5-23c7701c7a5e","30":"instance--913561d1-b5f3-54d2-8272-159233dfde54","330":"instance--d59fe52d-c897-5f3a-919a-c2273cb8a8b3","60":"instance--f1fd6a3d-bb83-543d-a379-39d4632978f7","90":"instance--4cd6fce2-0d24-57f0-b161-12a867cd1100","branch:False":"instance--f7e897b3-3607-5ea5-8d15-5f83ba8a60da","branch:True":"instance--39b5ac19-b0dd-5674-a7d9-d75e659fe9ea"},"id":"condition","instance":"attack-condition--1","properties":[["description","This array becomes the second stage of the infection process when it is executed."]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--2ff8b105-17d8-5bc8-9736-a71ca9281068","120":"instance--fe9b11f7-9a07-51c8-93b2-02f34148833b","150":"instance--15f0676c-2f2f-58cf-99a3-b5eade2d286e","180":"instance--cdc5e3d9-a0b4-5995-98a3-d1a29532ffb1","210":"instance--75ed5df8-ff2f-5667-9748-b8587a1ee318","30":"instance--46009917-4258-54e5-9e91-c46c4a45d34d","330":"instance--54845373-a5f0-5af0-b348-5b0a3b4fbe67","60":"instance--f1f8d9a5-1f2a-55c4-af9a-f2629bc0827a","90":"instance--ddfb6e54-4af9-5771-910f-b4c7ba6e9860","branch:False":"instance--64607b7d-a4bd-56e7-9116-7bc21201c8bf","branch:True":"instance--f635d174-aa29-531f-b9c8-0cc481c6c1dd"},"id":"condition","instance":"attack-condition--2","properties":[["description","If it determines that it is not being analyzed"]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--36aad375-d405-5e3b-9a7d-4346c75c9f45","120":"instance--acc72955-e581-59b3-80b5-35fb047df4b8","150":"instance--d5d0ec7c-da1b-5d39-86e4-8de8792ab05d","180":"instance--047e7862-d9c4-5716-b778-899a86595b48","210":"instance--650a6d3c-5cb0-5f82-83ec-c5d828e2502b","240":"instance--3f08654d-fd5e-59cb-af47-8bbcee29de39","270":"instance--e175549d-38ff-5527-bdb8-de5e1a12f356","30":"instance--c6e60459-b005-50cd-9e68-66ef210b5456","300":"instance--f90b34f0-8620-5a56-9e11-4db2b889aac4","330":"instance--93872aee-cf81-52fa-aa93-f7a84a833dbd","60":"instance--5a877a06-3649-5bba-9461-5faee75ea842","90":"instance--68af6616-0e27-5395-b4ff-5d95b55a2405"},"id":"OR_operator","instance":"attack-operator--1","properties":[["operator","OR"]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--fa24abb0-a9e2-57d1-9e9b-b0cd91186fea","120":"instance--b4681163-23aa-5b50-b8ae-78bec